\title{Weeknotes for 9 October 2026 (week 40)}
\date{2026-10-12}
\tag{weeknote}

\put\transclude/numbered{false}

\subtree{
  \title{Courses}

  \p{I have finally caught up on grading (\em{aka} marking), and I'm hoping to keep it that way.  I have a system for ensuring that I stay on top of grading as things get turned in throughout the semester; it's too boring to explain here but suffice it to say that it involves a spreadsheet and multiple [Beeminder](beeminder.com) goals.  It's a bit complicated, but the complication has evolved over several years in response to real issues, and it works pretty well, most of the time.  It kind of fell apart earlier in the semester due to some external factors, but now that I'm back on track I'm confident it will continue.}

  \p{[Algorithms](00JF) continues to go well; I am enjoying writing up my lecture notes in Forester.  The students just had their first exam, and overall they did pretty well. I give out the problems a week in advance, they can prepare however they want, and then they have to come in and write out their answers from memory in class, with no notes or technology.}
}

